§ `s 2(1)(b) -- which proceedings`

#ASSERT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `divorce`
#ASSERT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `nullity of marriage`
#ASSERT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `judicial separation`
#ASSERT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `restitution of conjugal rights`
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `a criminal trial`
#ASSERT NOT `the proceedings are matrimonial under section 2(1)(b)` `a maintenance or custody application`

§ `s 2(1)(b) -- the permitted particulars`

#ASSERT `the particular is in the permitted list` `the names of the parties`
#ASSERT `the particular is in the permitted list` `the address of a witness`
#ASSERT `the particular is in the permitted list` `the occupation of a party`
#ASSERT `the particular is in the permitted list` `a concise statement of a charge supported by evidence`
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is in the permitted list` `a charge on which no evidence was given`
#ASSERT `the particular is in the permitted list` `a submission on a point of law and the decision on it`
#ASSERT `the particular is in the permitted list` `the decision and the court's observations`
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is in the permitted list` `a witness's testimony in detail`
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is in the permitted list` `the name of a child who did not testify`
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is in the permitted list` `the ages of the parties`
#ASSERT NOT `the particular is in the permitted list` `a photograph of a party`

§ `s 2(2) -- indecency overrides the permitted list`

#ASSERT `the particular may be reported` `divorce` `the names of the parties` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the particular may be reported` `divorce` `the names of the parties` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the particular may be reported` `divorce` `a photograph of a party` FALSE
#ASSERT `the particular may be reported` `a criminal trial` `a photograph of a party` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the particular may be reported` `nullity of marriage` `the decision and the court's observations` TRUE

§ `ss 2 and 5 -- contravention and savings`

#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a divorce report naming the parties and the decision`
#ASSERT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a divorce report quoting the testimony`
#ASSERT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a judicial separation report naming a child`
#ASSERT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a nullity report with indecent details`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a criminal trial report quoting the testimony`
#ASSERT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a criminal trial report with indecent details`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a maintenance application report with the evidence`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a law report of a divorce case with the full evidence`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a medical journal article with indecent physiological details`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a notice of a divorce published as the court directed`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a transcript printed for the parties`
#ASSERT NOT `the publication contravenes section 2` `a magazine story with indecent matter about no case`

§ `s 3 -- who can be convicted`

#ASSERT `the person may be convicted` `a divorce report quoting the testimony` `the editor`
#ASSERT `the person may be convicted` `a divorce report quoting the testimony` `the printer`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may be convicted` `a divorce report quoting the testimony` `the reporter who wrote it`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may be convicted` `a divorce report quoting the testimony` `a party who supplied the details`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may be convicted` `a divorce report naming the parties and the decision` `the publisher`

§ `s 4 -- Public Prosecutor's consent`

#ASSERT `a prosecution may be commenced` `a criminal trial report with indecent details` `the proprietor` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a prosecution may be commenced` `a criminal trial report with indecent details` `the proprietor` FALSE

§ `s 3 -- penalty`

#ASSERT `the maximum fine in dollars` EQUALS 1000

#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment in months` EQUALS 12

#ASSERT `the sentence is within section 3` 1000 12
#ASSERT NOT `the sentence is within section 3` 1001 0
#ASSERT NOT `the sentence is within section 3` 0 13

